My best Rogue game ever, ended to a combo of surprise and stupidity.
Orcish rogue.

Level 3 gave me a displacement cloak.  Cursed -1, but I didn't mind.
Level 4 had a general store with a shield of reflection.  Pretty good
start, eh?  I went down a bit, then over to the Mines down to Town
(friendly temple!), then back to the Dungeons, down to level 11 (wizard
bones [killed by spellcasting exhaustion!?] gave me magic resistance and
water walking boots), Sokoban for the bag of holding, back to the Mines
for the luckstone.  Luckstones, as it turned out, plus healthstone.  I
was accumulating lots of daggers, but I also got a pleasant surprise in
the temple:

An object appears at your feet!
A - a baseball bat called the Bat out of Hell

Well, I looked that up... baseball bats are a nicer club, and the Bat
out of Hell is +20 damage all around.  Holy daggers, that's better than
Mjollnir!

Later on I got Houchou, the instakilling spoon.

I never actually stole much from shopkeepers, though I did kill a
couple.  I forgot how tough they were in slashem, but I had two potions
of invulnerability and the Bat.  I left a general store owner alive in
the Mall for ID purposes.

I found found Grund but stayed away.  I feared gelatinous cubes but
could dagger or wand of striking them.  I found one enchant (armor)
scroll in the whole game, though I had a blessed scroll of genocide from
early on.

So, finally I tried the Quest.  I had a scare with an "arch-lich"
(chameleon) and started using, possibly for the first time in any game
ever, the ring of protection from shapechangers.  Very nice when you're
surrounded by chameleons.  I explored down to the bottom of the Quest,
then retreated up to the Mall to identify my loot, which included a ring
of free action and a wand of polymorph.

"The engraving looks different."

*wait, I've seen that before.  Let me look... hmm, that's really
polymorph; I thought the early message change was rather minimal.  So
what are those two wands I was calling polymorph?*

"The yellow mold looks weaker."

*oh.  Glad I didn't try using those on myself.*

So I returned and xornified so I could penetrate the closet above the
main level.  I quickly got frozen by a guardian naga, which was a new
experience.  I figured later that's blocked by magic resistance, but
xorns can't wear cloaks.  I survived that, thinking I needed my ring of
free action, but had a lot of ring juggling -- poly control, prot from
shape changers, see invisible (still didn't have the intrisic), free
action.  I went down to the Nemesis level, discovered there are *four*
separate sections, not two, and that the nagas in the main section
follow you quite assiduously.  I grabbed the tin of chameleon meat not
that I needed it, drank a potion of speed, and outran the nagas to get
some space as I broke into the main chamber.  The Master Assassin woke
up, I hit him with the Bat, he ran off.  Yay...

But I'd forgotten to swap free action for poly control after the last
polymorph, and before I could change back and put my cloak on I got
frozen by the nagas.  They bit me until I changed back to an orc, froze
me again, and bit me to final death.

So... damn.  That game was almost a perfect setup, and I blew it.

Later I thought that it might be best to pop in just long enough to wake
up the Master, then pull back to deal with him.  There's probably
nothing in the cavern worth tangling with a zillion guardian nagas and a
golden naga if you don't have free action or magic resistance on.

